cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use T1DUJxUoM in academic work, please cite the archived software release and the source-code repository using the metadata below."

title: "T1DUJxUoM: Forecasting Accuracy Is Not Enough — Safety-Oriented Evaluation of Neural Digital Twins Before In-Silico Insulin and Carbohydrate Intervention in Type 1 Diabetes"
type: software

abstract: "T1DUJxUoM is the reproducibility companion for a six-configuration ablation of physiology-guided LSTM digital twins for Type 1 Diabetes, evaluated across two independent cohorts (University of Manchester T1D-UOM and OhioT1DM) and five random seeds under a strict 60/20/20 chronological train/validation/test split. It includes the training pipeline (direct glucose prediction, stochastic glucose masking, corrected raw-space double-monotonicity loss), evaluation scripts (multi-horizon rollout RMSE, naive-persistence and Ridge-AR baselines, insulin/carbohydrate dose-response audit, and an in-silico counterfactual scenario panel), a regression test guarding a previously fixed raw-space perturbation defect, and configuration files needed to reproduce the tables and figures in the accompanying paper. It supersedes and replaces the results reported in the earlier T1DUJxUoM v3.0.0 (10.5281/zenodo.18434352) and v4.0.0 (10.5281/zenodo.20693048) releases, which used a different evaluation split and, for v4.0.0, an implementation defect in the monotonicity-penalty perturbation later identified and corrected."

